    "intro": "SCHOLARSHIPS AND EDUCATION LOAN FOR JAIN MINORITY STUDENTS! The population of Jains in our country is less than 0.4% yet they stand ahead in contributing the most to the Indian economy. Jains were given the status of a “minority religion” by the Government of India, as per Section 2(c) of the National Commission for Minorities (NCM) Act (NCM), 1992. The Jain community is one of India’s most prosperous groups. They have become a prosperous community through years of hard work and an understanding of business. However, not everyone in the community is financially secure, and this sparked the interest of several influential community members. The Jain community decided to assist students who have the academic potential to achieve greater heights but are unable to do so due to financial constraints. In addition, the ministry of minority affairs has established a few scholarships for minority students. The Jain community and the ministry of minority affairs offer the following scholarships for Jain students:",
